{
  "$comment": [
    "MEASURED against production (project ixvwfbuvfxxsjiywhbbb) on 2026-09-09, not derived",
    "from supabase/migrations/. Those files describe a different lineage than the live",
    "database (see docs/DB-HARDENING-AUDIT.md), so the catalog is the only honest source.",
    "Re-measure with `node scripts/check-rls.mjs`, or with the SQL in docs/AUTH-MODEL.md.",
    "src/lib/auth/rls-manifest.test.ts is the CI gate that reads this file."
  ],
  "measured_at": "2026-09-09",
  "reverified_at": "2026-09-09",
  "$reverified_comment": "Re-measured against production on 2026-09-09 after 21 days of drift. 53 tables -> 81, and the shape of a locked table changed: the eight ZERO-POLICY tables now carry an explicit deny_all_client_roles policy (USING false, WITH CHECK false) instead. That is the same denial written down rather than inferred, so service_role_only now accepts either shape and the gate checks the predicates, not just the count. payment_webhook_events left the list: it gained an is_admin() SELECT policy and is no longer service-role-only for reading. wallet_balances and wallet_transactions LOST their is_admin() INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE policies and now carry a SELECT policy only, so the money ledger is no longer writable through PostgREST by any client role.",
  "project_ref": "ixvwfbuvfxxsjiywhbbb",
  "schema": "public",
  "service_role_only": {
    "$comment": [
      "Tables no client role may touch at all. TWO SHAPES SATISFY THIS, and both are checked.",
      "(1) Zero policies. Postgres denies every row to every non-superuser role when RLS is on",
      "and no policy matches, so the table is reachable only by the service key and by SECURITY",
      "DEFINER functions. (2) An explicit `deny_all_client_roles` policy for {anon,authenticated}",
      "with USING false and WITH CHECK false, which is the same denial stated out loud.",
      "Production moved from (1) to (2) between 2026-08-19 and 2026-09-09. Adding any OTHER",
      "policy here to satisfy the advisor's rls_enabled_no_policy INFO would LOOSEN the table,",
      "and the gate fails on exactly that: a policy on this list that is not the deny-all shape."
    ],
    "legacy_percent_archive_112": "frozen pre-112 commission snapshot; nobody reads it at runtime",
    "rate_limits": "counters, reached only through the SECURITY DEFINER check_rate_limit()",
    "referral_signals": "raw attribution signals; aggregated into referrals before anyone sees them",
    "search_index_dlq": "failed index jobs; drained by the cron route on CRON_SECRET",
    "search_index_outbox": "pending index jobs; enqueued by triggers and drained by the cron route on CRON_SECRET",
    "settlement_events": "money ledger; written by settlement code, never by a browser",
    "stock_reservations": "held by the checkout server path and reaped by cron",
    "user_rate_limits": "per-user counters for check_user_rate_limit(), which is not granted to authenticated"
  },
