    "$no_write_policy_means": "RLS is on and no policy grants the command, so Postgres denies it for every non-superuser role. Writes reach these tables only through the service role or a SECURITY DEFINER function. That is the tightest state available, not a gap. Since 2026-09-09 this list includes wallet_balances and wallet_transactions, whose is_admin() write policies were dropped in production: the ledger is now append-only from the client's side too.",
