        "UPDATE": 1,
        "DELETE": 1
      }
    },
    "intended": {
      "carts": "anon and authenticated both write carts by design: a guest cart exists before there is an account. This is the only relation where a client role SHOULD hold DML and does."
    },
    "column_grants": {
      "notifications.read_at": "The bell marks itself read through a column grant rather than a table grant, so nothing else on the row is writable. Read from pg_attribute.attacl: information_schema.role_column_grants PROJECTS a table-level grant onto every column and cannot tell a real column grant from an inherited one.",
      "reviews.supplier_reply, reviews.supplier_replied_at, reviews.supplier_replied_by": "Same shape: a supplier may write its reply onto a review it cannot otherwise touch."
    },
    "$surplus_means": "The client role holds a DML privilege AND no PERMISSIVE policy grants any client role INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE or ALL. With RLS on and no permissive write policy Postgres refuses the write before the grant is consulted, so every one of these privileges is unusable today and is revoked by migrations/pending/230_revoke_surplus_client_dml.sql. Revoking cannot break a working code path; what it buys is that a future policy written permissive by accident is inert instead of live.",
